flow "Hedged requests"
summary "Sends a backup request to another replica after a short tail-latency delay to cut p99 latency, risking duplicate load under saturation."
tags latency resilience tail-latency
level intermediate
source "https://research.google/pubs/the-tail-at-scale/"
related distributed-systems/timeouts-deadline-propagation distributed-systems/retry-backoff-dlq

node client "Client" actor
node caller "Frontend" service tone=primary
group replicas "Read replicas"
node r1 "Replica 1" service in=replicas
node r2 "Replica 2" service in=replicas
edge client > caller
edge caller > r1
edge caller > r2

scenario hedge "Hedged backup cuts p99 tail latency"
  step send-first "Send primary request to Replica 1"
    "The client reads an idempotent endpoint. Frontend sends the request to Replica 1 and starts a timer at the **p95 latency** threshold (10ms)."
    send client > caller "GET /profile"
    state caller active
    send caller > r1 "req #1"
    state r1 warning
    callout r1 "Slow: GC pause (120ms)"
  step send-hedge "Timer fires at 10ms: hedge to Replica 2"
    "Replica 1 has not answered after 10ms. Instead of waiting 120ms for the slow tail, Frontend sends a duplicate **hedged** request to Replica 2."
    detail "Deferring the backup request until the expected 95th-percentile latency keeps extra load tiny. In Google's Bigtable benchmark (reading 1,000 keys across 100 servers), waiting 10ms before hedging cut 99.9th-percentile latency from 1,800ms down to 74ms for only 2% more total requests."
    send caller > r2 "hedge #1"
    state r2 active
  step winner "Replica 2 responds fast; cancel Replica 1"
    "Replica 2 replies in 3ms. Frontend returns the fast answer immediately (13ms total instead of 120ms) and cancels the slow call on Replica 1."
    send r2 > caller "200 OK (3ms)"
    send caller > client "200 OK (13ms)"
    send caller > r1 "cancel" with
    state caller,r2 success
    callout caller "p99 cut from 120ms -> 13ms"

scenario duplicate-load "Global overload turns hedging into 2x load" from=hedge/send-first
  step both-slow "Both replicas are saturated"
    "During a traffic spike, **every** replica slows past 10ms. Now almost every single incoming request fires a hedged copy."
    state r1,r2 error
    effect r1,r2 shake
    send caller > r1 "100% QPS"
    send caller > r2 "+100% hedged QPS!" with
    callout r2 "Cluster load doubles (2x)!"
  step budget "Cap hedging with a token budget"
    "Unbounded hedging accelerates collapse when the whole fleet is busy. Production systems cap hedges at **~5-10%** of traffic via a token bucket so hedging shuts off during overload."
    detail "For example, gRPC's per-server `retryThrottling` bucket starts at `maxTokens`, subtracts `1` on failures/hedges, adds `tokenRatio` on successes, and pauses hedging and retries whenever `token_count` drops below `maxTokens / 2`."
    state caller warning
    callout caller "Hedging budget: max 10% extra QPS"
